# Node: equal.ByBuiltinRule.Calculation.ClosedDecimal (complex nested closed trees)
# Nested closed-numeric calculation mixing arithmetic, integer ops, foldable
# sqrt/log, and known_closed_numeric_equal rewrite.
# Run: LITEX_NEW_PIPELINE=1 litex -f examples/new_pipeline/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/calculation_closed_decimal_complex_nested.lit
#
# See also: calculation_closed_decimal.lit, calculation_closed_decimal_arithmetic_ops.lit,
#           calculation_closed_decimal_integer_sqrt_log.lit
# Owned by: ClosedNumericExpr + evaluate_obj_to_normalized_decimal_number
#           (+ sqrt_decimal_str_and_normalize / log_integer_power_decimal_str).
# Boundary: any non-foldable hole (sqrt(2), free `a`, 2.5 % 1) still fails closed calc.

# Nested arithmetic + integer + foldable sqrt/log
gcd(54, (-24)) + 3! = 12
sqrt(4) * log(2, 8) + floor(2.5)! = 8
lcm(12, 18) / gcd(12, 18) = 6
((-7) % 3)^log(2, 4) + sqrt(0.36) = 4.6
ceil(sqrt(0.36) + 1.1) * 3! = 12
abs(min(-2, 3)) + max(sign(-4), 1) * quot(17, 5) = 5
min(max(2^3, 3!), gcd(54, 24)) = 6

# Multi-name rewrite then nested residual
have a N = 3!
have b R = sqrt(4)
have c R = log(2, 8)
a + b * c = 12
abs(a - b^c) + gcd(a, 4) = 4
